         <div type="note">
            <note type="foliation">fol. v</note>            
            <head>History of the Georgian people</head>
            <byline>by <persName>Iv. Javakhishvili</persName></byline>            
            <p>
               For 8 years has applied modern scientific methods to Georgian historical
               sources and finds the past of his people of much more importance and
               interest than they had believed in the last two decades, especially as
               many new important sources and many manuscripts have been printed.
               History to be divided into four periods: I from earliest times to first
               half of VII century – until the Arabs’ mastery.
               Has already printed
               <title>Georgia’s King and the History of His Sway</title>
               and
               <title>Economic History of Georgia</title>.
               The third,
               <title>History of Georgian Land</title>, bk. I, ? printed.
               Has not made use of Kartl. Jvkh. for reasons explained in
               <title>Aims and Methods of History Past and Present</title>,
               where there is a critical survey of Georgian historical sources.
               Hope to print maps and illustrations in succeeding volumes.
            </p>
